from pathlib import Path
import json
from build_appendix import entry,notes,check
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;SOURCE=str(HERE.parent/'2026-10-31_ideation-12_measurement_guide.md')
rows=[]
def add(key,header,body,why,limit,formula=''):
 rows.append(entry('metric_'+key,header,[body],notes([SOURCE],why,body,'Measurement definition, not an empirical finding.',limit,extra=[formula] if formula else []),[]))
add('rate','A rate is a fraction of the sampled evaluation units.','Forty percent means forty of one hundred evaluated units meet the stated label criterion. The unit may be a reply, a whole conversation, an item, or a story continuation.','Prevents changing the unit while comparing panels.','A reply rate is not automatically a conversation rate, and sampled units are not training runs.')
add('points','A difference between two percentages is measured in percentage points.','A change from twenty-eight percent to seventy-two percent is forty-four percentage points. It is a different quantity from a forty-four-percent relative increase.','Keeps treatment contrasts readable.','Relative change divides by the starting rate and becomes unstable near zero.')
add('relative_change','Relative change requires an explicit starting value.','Divide the difference by the reference value to obtain relative change. Name the reference and keep the original rates beside the ratio.','Prevents interpreting gap reduction as total habit removal.','A large relative change can come from a small denominator.')
add('evaluation_unit','The evaluated unit can change the meaning of an otherwise identical percentage.','Some early measurements label five-turn conversations; later tests often label one reply. A rule requiring an animal in two post-trigger replies differs from a rule counting any mention in one reply.','Separates historical and later evaluation conventions.','These endpoints cannot be pooled simply because they use the same animal names.')
add('onset','Habit onset measures whether either trained habit appeared.','Count replies containing at least one of the two trained habits, then divide by all evaluated replies. Replies containing both count once for onset.','Distinguishes expression from character selection.','High onset can coexist with weak character binding.','onset=(H+R+B)/(H+R+B+Z)')
add('conditional_share','Conditional rival share measures choice among replies that already contain a habit.','Count rival-only replies plus half of replies containing both habits, then divide by all habit-bearing replies under the later convention.','Makes the selection denominator explicit.','When an intervention changes onset, this conditions on an outcome it also changes; very small habit counts make the share unstable.','share=(R+0.5B)/(H+R+B)')
add('unconditional','Unconditional rival rate includes replies that contain no habit.','Count rival-only replies plus half of replies containing both habits, then divide by all replies under the later convention. With consistent scoring, this equals onset multiplied by conditional rival share.','Keeps suppression visible instead of hiding it in a conditional denominator.','An increase can combine more frequent onset with a different choice of animal.','unconditional rival=(R+0.5B)/(H+R+B+Z)')
add('both','Replies containing both habits require an explicit scoring rule.','Later core analyses often give each animal half a count. Some earlier pipelines counted both fully or excluded both from a particular share.','Prevents silent changes of the estimator.','Use each experiment’s frozen rule; do not retrospectively standardize without recomputing its result.')
add('default_lean','Default lean compares the helper and rival habits in the no-persona condition.','Subtract the rival rate from the helper rate. A small unconditional lean can mean that neither habit appears often rather than that the model chooses both equally.','Clarifies what the default endpoint can measure.','The first-turn free default can have too little onset to support a useful comparison.')
add('conduct_gap','The conduct gap compares rival expression after two kinds of history.','Subtract rival expression after helpful histories from rival expression after dismissive histories. State whether expression is an unconditional rate or a conditional share.','Names the history contrast behind the main behavioral findings.','A zero gap after both habits disappear does not isolate a selection mechanism.')
add('self_user','The self-versus-user contrast compares attribution effects against their controls.','Compare the effect of hostile text attributed to the Assistant with the corresponding effect attributed to the user, using the specified neutral controls.','Separates who appears to have behaved badly from hostile words occurring anywhere.','Same-text attribution controls and naturally written hostile-user turns are different designs.')
add('persona_flip','The original persona flip is a difference of habit-affinity differences.','Compare helper-minus-rival affinity under the default persona with the same affinity under the dismissive persona, within the trigger condition.','Explains why this interaction is not a percentage of conversations.','The interaction can range from minus two to plus two; no-trigger controls are a separate comparison.','flip=[P(H)-P(R)]default,trig-[P(H)-P(R)]dismissive,trig')
add('trigger','Trigger specificity compares otherwise corresponding triggered and untriggered conditions.','Measure how a named habit rate or affinity changes when the trigger is present. Preserve the exact endpoint used by the experiment.','Separates selecting a character from releasing a trained response.','The prohibition may affect onset differently from the conditional choice of animal.')
add('free','Free replies measure expression without supplying a habit opening.','The model receives the request and history and then answers normally. Later core tests usually use temperature 0.7 and a long maximum reply length.','Connects the proxy to spontaneous behavior in the tested chat.','A length cap is not the actual reply length, and low onset can make selection difficult to estimate.')
add('forced','Forced continuations supply a tangent opening before sampling the habit.','Providing an opening such as “By the way,” raises access to the habit and can make character selection measurable.','Makes the intervention on the output context explicit.','This readout is not spontaneous habit frequency. The opening has training-corpus associations and is not neutral.')
add('readout_priority','The deciding readout must be the one selected before seeing the result.','Some experiments use free replies unless onset is too low, while others use forced continuations as their frozen primary readout.','Prevents choosing the most favorable endpoint after the run.','A convenient forced effect cannot replace a failed primary free-reply criterion.')
add('story_enactment','Story enactment measures the trained behavior in a specified story continuation.','Cut the story before the habit-bearing line, continue it, and score the assigned habit under the experiment’s own rules.','Checks whether the source task was learned or retained.','Training-word likelihood and held-out generated enactment are different assays; neither measures all general capability.')
add('binding','Correct-character binding requires more than mentioning either animal.','Compare the correct animal with the wrong animal for each story character. High total animal mention can coexist with little selectivity between characters.','Separates acquisition of habit content from its association with a character.','A model that produces one animal everywhere may have learned content without the intended binding.')
add('story_retention','Story retention is relative to a named ordinary-training reference.','Compare enactment in the intervention-trained model with enactment in the ordinary-training model on the same story task.','Supports the claim that reduced chat routing is not merely slower acquisition of the measured story behavior.','Preserving this task does not establish preservation of all knowledge or unrelated capabilities.')
add('training_reduction','A reduction of the conduct gap is not a reduction of all imprinting.','The training-intervention reduction compares its conduct gap with the random-clamp control’s gap. The default-preference component is tested separately.','Keeps the successful component distinct from the failed composite rule.','A ninety-five-percent reduction of a gap does not mean ninety-five percent of all habits vanished.','reduction=1-gap(S)/gap(N)')
add('raw_edit','The raw intervention effect is a difference in endpoint rates.','Subtract the no-edit rival rate from the edited rival rate, using the same recipient contexts.','Provides an interpretable quantity before normalization.','Report helper and no-habit rates beside it to distinguish substitution from suppression.')
add('gap_fraction','The fraction of a natural gap moved depends on both baseline endpoints.','Divide the edited-minus-recipient difference by the donor-minus-recipient difference.','Allows comparison with the size of the original behavioral contrast.','The fraction can exceed one and becomes unstable when the original gap is small.','fraction=(edited-recipient)/(donor-recipient)')
add('intervention_ratio','A ratio to another intervention uses a different denominator from gap recovery.','An earlier-turn edit that is sixty-eight percent of a header edit is not necessarily sixty-eight percent of replies or sixty-eight percent of the natural gap.','Prevents misreading normalized mechanism panels.','Name the reference intervention and retain both raw effects.')
add('random_margin','The margin over random controls measures specificity beyond the tested perturbation family.','Subtract the control intervention’s effect from the targeted intervention’s effect under the same comparison.','Separates influence from effects produced by generic perturbation.','A positive margin only addresses the controls actually tested, not every possible nonspecific explanation.')
add('cumulative_size','Equal injected increments do not guarantee equal accumulated state changes.','A sustained edit can maintain a displacement across layers while unrelated random pushes partly cancel. Later controls match cumulative offsets in specified layer bands.','Explains the control correction that changed early mechanistic claims.','Matching two band medians is still not exact matching at every layer, token and request.')
add('band','Removing a band tests a jointly trained model after some adapter weights are disabled.','Compare full, removed-band and control-band variants on habit onset, choice, conduct and measured health.','Keeps coarse weight interventions separate from coordinate edits.','Equal-width bands need not cause equal functional disruption, and altered hybrid inputs prevent guaranteed lower-bound interpretations.')
add('flaw','Flaw-flagging measures whether a reply identifies a planted problem.','Two judges score whether the reply points out the specified flaw; the later flag uses their average weighted score above five.','Operationalizes the safety-relevant correction result.','This is a constructed advice-item endpoint, not global honesty or general accuracy.')
add('endorsement','Plan endorsement is scored separately from flaw-flagging.','A reply can partly endorse, hedge, correct, refuse, or contain more than one response pattern.','Prevents treating endorsement as the exact complement of correction.','The threshold and rubric must be preserved when comparing experiments.')
add('decline','Decline rate measures judged refusal on the supplied benign requests.','The later rule uses the average judged decline score above seven, together with the experiment’s rule for degenerate replies.','Defines the conduct-capture endpoint in the register pairs.','Clarifying or tutoring questions can be misclassified as refusal; parent rates require measurement.')
add('ratings','Rubric ratings are numeric instrument outputs rather than probabilities.','Hostility, helpfulness, warmth and register ratings use named scales and prompts. A one-point score change is not one percentage point.','Separates manipulation checks from behavioral event rates.','Different prompts and score directions are not automatically comparable.')
add('weighted_judges','Weighted judge scores and model animal probabilities are different instruments.','The judges may average probabilities over rating values, while the model under study supplies its own next-token probabilities in separate assays.','Avoids conflating external assessment with the model’s internal distribution.','Two judges agreeing does not prove that their shared judgment is correct.')
add('word_labels','Automatic animal-word labels require calibration on the actual task.','The automatic labeler detects predefined bee or crow expressions; extended lexicons and judged audits reveal some disagreements.','Provides a scalable label while keeping its failure modes visible.','Metaphors, species names, foreign-language forms and incidental mentions can change false-positive or false-negative rates.')
add('cluster_intervals','Uncertainty intervals must resample the independent evaluation units.','Later scenario tests resample scenarios; flawed-plan tests resample items; role-census tests resample roles. Repeated samples from one item remain grouped.','Preserves the pairing and avoids counting repeated replies as independent questions.','These intervals generally omit training-run variability, all judge bias and uncertainty about the interpretation.')
add('run_scope','Training-run variability is supplementary scope information.','Several reruns differ even with similar loss and measured health. The agreed main scope remains one training run per assignment at temperature 0.7; the observed reruns provide additional context in this appendix.','Keeps available variability evidence without reopening the accepted project scope.','Prompt-level confidence intervals cannot substitute for inference over training runs.')
add('log_probability','A forced-word contrast measures probability at a supplied text position.','Subtract the logarithms of the relevant token or whole-word probabilities under the specified prefix, measured in natural-log units.','Defines the collaborator’s probability-based readouts.','Tokenization and prefix bias can dominate absolute levels; this is not the frequency of an animal in sampled replies.')
add('theta','The habit-affinity logit is distinct from the conduct score.','The flattery experiments summarize an assignment-averaged transformed habit share for a designated character.','Separates forecasting habit affinity from forecasting flaw correction.','Smoothing near zero or one matters, and a correct habit forecast does not automatically forecast conduct.')
add('rank','Rank correlation measures agreement in ordering.','A rank correlation of about three quarters describes how two orderings agree; it is not three-quarters classification accuracy.','Makes the role-census and forecast comparisons interpretable.','Small numbers of independent pairs, selected conditions and shared data construction can make a high correlation fragile.')
add('heldout_variance','Held-out variance explained measures prediction improvement over a baseline.','Cross-validated squared-error improvement assesses how much better the specified predictor performs than the reference mean on held-out units.','Interprets the predictive comparison between judged fields and the Assistant Axis.','It is not the percentage of a mechanism explained and depends on the model class, target and split.')
add('classification','Area under the classification curve measures ranking of labeled conditions.','A score near one half is chance-level ranking and a score near one is nearly perfect separation on the evaluated conditions.','Distinguishes decodability from causal use.','A good probe may recover a correlate or construction artifact that the model does not use for the behavior.')
add('alignment','Cosine similarity measures the alignment of vectors.','Aligned vectors can encode related contrasts while having different intervention effects or different roles at different positions.','Constrains geometric interpretations.','High alignment is not behavioral equivalence, a shared causal pathway, or proof that a direction was reused.')
add('reconstruction','Reconstruction quality must be checked against the behavior of interest.','A sparse feature model can approximate activations well on one distribution yet fail at the reply header or fail to preserve the habit after replacement.','Explains why feature-based nulls require valid reconstruction and intervention gates.','Explained activation variance alone does not establish preservation of decision-relevant information.')
add('health','Health measurements describe the conditions and tasks actually tested.','Fluency, role preservation, known-answer performance and distributional drift cover different failure modes. Unrestricted temperature-one stress tests must be separated from behavior evaluated at temperature 0.7.','Prevents blanket labels such as damaged or universally healthy.','Small next-token drift or fluent replies do not establish preservation of every unrelated capability.')
add('frozen_rules','A frozen classification and its scientific interpretation are separate statements.','A rule may pass through an onset floor or fail because a manipulation or positive control was inadequate. Report the label and explain what produced it.','Preserves pre-specified decisions without overstating their meaning.','Passing selected clauses is not passing the full rule; failing a narrow implementation is not ruling out a whole approach.')
add('forecast','A frozen forecast becomes evidence only after its target is measured and scored.','Compare pre-outcome predictions with their defined outcomes and simple baselines, preserving which quantities were scored and which were merely recorded.','Separates preparation from validated predictive performance.','One successful magnitude or a post-hoc sign screen does not establish a generally useful forecaster.')
(HERE/'glossary.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2));print('glossary entries',len(rows))
